  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\left(1+x+x^{2}\\right)^{9}=a_{0}+a_{1} x+a_{2} x^{2}$\r\n$+\\ldots+a_{18} x^{18} \\cdot$ Then"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$a_{0}+a_{2}+\\ldots+a_{18}=a_{1}+a_{3}+\\ldots+a_{17}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$a_{0}+a_{2}+\\ldots+a_{18}$ is even",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$a_{0}+a_{2}+\\ldots+a_{18}$ is divisible by 9",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$a_{0}+a_{2}+\\ldots+a_{18}$ is divisible by 3 but not by 9",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\left(1+x+x^{2}\\right)^{9}=a_{0}+a_{1} x+a_{2} x^{2}+ \\dots+a_{18}x^{18}$\r\n$$\r\nPut $x=-1,$ we get\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n(1-1+1)^{9}=a_{0}-a_{1}+a_{2}+\\ldots+a_{18} \\\\\r\n\\Rightarrow 1=a_{0}-a_{1}+a_{2}+\\ldots+a_{18}\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$\r\nPut $x=1,$ we get\r\n$$\r\n(1+1+1)^{9}=a_{0}+a_{1}+a_{2}+\\ldots+a_{14}\r\n$$\r\n$\\Rightarrow 3^{9}=a_{0}+a_{1}+a_{2}+\\ldots+a_{18}$\r\nOn adding Eqs. (i) and (ii), we get\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{c}\r\n3^{9}+1=2\\left(a_{0}+a_{2}+\\ldots+a_{10}\\right) \\\\\r\na_{0}+a_{2}+a_{4}+\\ldots+a_{18}=\\frac{3^{0}+1}{2} \\\\\r\n=\\frac{19683+1}{2} \\\\\r\n=\\frac{19684}{2}\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$\r\n$=9842$ which is even number."
  }
